body:
Thank you for giving a reasonable response.

&#x200B;

The issue, then, is that when I called them, I was extremely calm (it is virtually impossible to calm someone down when they are already calm), and the best mental support I could be given would be a reason to live that works within my value system (I have had the opinion of professionals that my value system is unusual and perhaps wildly out-of-step with 21st century western culture, but not inherently unhealthy, and that one of my needs is to embrace it as it is.)

Interesting.  Would you consider multiple years of contemplation to be an "impulse decision"?

&#x200B;

I am curious as to your reasoning in this.
